course: dictionary
lesson: 8821
title: The Shema
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The Shema is a prayer, and it is one of the most important prayers in the Jewish faith. Its name comes from its first word, «Hear». Many Jews say it every morning and evening, so it is a prayer they say every day.
explain: The Shema begins «Hear, O Israel: the Lord is our God, the Lord is one.» The words show the Jewish belief in one God. Read the words around «Shema» as context: they tell you it is a prayer about God.
explain: The Shema is a noun, so it names a thing. When someone says «say the Shema» or «recite the Shema», they mean say this prayer out loud.
fact: The Shema is the most important Jewish prayer.
fact: «Shema» is a Hebrew word, and its first word, «Hear», is what the prayer starts with.
fact: The Shema comes from the book of Deuteronomy in the Bible.
fact: Its words are written inside the mezuzah on doorposts and in tefillin.
fact: The Shema teaches that God is one, and that people should love God with all their heart, soul and strength.
exercise: What is the Shema? | *The most important Jewish prayer | A Jewish holiday with lights | A special type of bread | A book of the Bible about kings
exercise: Which word in «Hear, O Israel: the Lord is our God, the Lord is one» tells people to listen? | Lord | One | Israel | *Hear
exercise: Where are the words of the Shema written? | Inside a sealed jar in the sea | *Inside a mezuzah on a doorpost | On a school whiteboard | On the front of a church bell
test: How often do many Jews say the Shema? | *Every morning and evening | Only on Saturdays | Never | Once a year
test: Which book of the Bible does the Shema come from? | *Deuteronomy | Exodus | Psalms | Genesis
exam: Which word could replace «say» in «say the Shema» and keep the same meaning? | ignore | eat | *recite | forget
